# TEMPLATE: multi-topic source. Courses, long masterclasses, general ecommerce books.
#
# File it in 99-multi when 4 or more modules get REAL coverage and none dominates.
# If 1 module clearly dominates, use that module's folder instead, even if 3 others
# appear in passing.
#
# Filename: MULTI_YYYY-MM-DD_author-slug_topic-slug.md
#
# IT STAYS AS 1 FILE. Do not cut a 4 hour course into 7 files. The context around a
# claim is what gives the claim its conditions, and splitting by hand destroys it.
# The pipeline segments by meaning and routes each segment to its own module.
#
# THE covers: BLOCK is the point of this template. Roughly 2 minutes while you skim.
# It gives the segmenter human anchors, which beat anything it can infer, and the
# ranges you mark "skip" get discarded without a model having to decide.
#
# Format: [start-end]  MODULE / topic     or     [start-end]  what it is, skip
# Use the same timestamp format as the transcript. Approximate is fine.
#
# Worked example:
#   modules: [MEA, MCR, ADC, OFF, COG]
#   covers:
#     - [00:00-22:15]     generic intro, skip
#     - [22:15-48:00]     MEA / attribution windows and restatement
#     - [48:00-1:19:00]   MCR / hook types and fatigue
#     - [1:19:00-1:52:00] ADC / account structure by spend band
#     - [1:52:00-2:20:00] OFF / guarantee structures, thin
#     - [2:20:00-3:05:00] COG / supplier negotiation, strongest section
#     - [3:05:00-4:02:00] outro and pitch, skip
#
# The receipt will tell you which ranges actually produced cards, so over time you
# learn which parts of a long course were worth the hours.
#
# LEAVE covers: OUT ENTIRELY if you do not have the 2 minutes. The pipeline still
# segments and routes correctly. It is an accelerant, not a requirement.
#
